  "schoolyard_use_notes": "This tree has striking clusters of bright, brush-like flowers that can introduce students to pollination and attract various pollinators. Its evergreen leaves provide a year-round example of photosynthesis and leaf structure. The bark peels in long strips, offering a tactile way to explore tree growth and bark texture. The woody seed capsules can be used to discuss seed dispersal and plant reproduction.",
